PREFACE

  No. 4 of 2003

  Penalties Act, 2003

  An Act to prescribe the penalties applicable to offences under the laws of Atlantis; to consolidate and amend the schedule of fines, imprisonment terms and community service orders; and for connected purposes.

PREAMBLE

  BE IT ENACTED by the Assembly of Atlantis, and by the authority of the same, as follows:

BODY

SECTION 1 - Short title

  This Act may be cited as the Penalties Act, 2003.

SECTION 2 - Interpretation

  In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires, "the Schedule" means the Schedule of Penalties set out in section 4 and "prescribed penalty" means the penalty specified in the Schedule for the offence in question.

SECTION 3 - Application of prescribed penalties

  SUBSECTION (1)

    Where an offence is specified in the Schedule, the court shall, upon conviction, impose a penalty not exceeding the prescribed penalty for that offence.

  SUBSECTION (2)

    The court may, having regard to the circumstances of the case and the character of the offender, impose a lesser penalty than the prescribed penalty.

SECTION 4 - Schedule of penalties

  The following penalties apply to the offences specified:

